& [Server]
  + separate crate and binary cantor-compiler-mcp
  + stdio transport only and no arguments
  + exactly one advertised tool validate_native_lifecycle

& [Arguments]
  + closed object with exactly request
  + request deserializes as NativeLifecycleValidationRequest and retains every nested deny-unknown-field rule
  + serialized MCP argument size is at most core request bound plus 65536 bytes of wrapper allowance

& [Dispatch]
  + call validate_native_lifecycle_request exactly once with the typed supplied request
  + do not derive repair normalize sign persist execute or reinterpret lifecycle forms
  + structuredContent equals serialized NativeLifecycleValidationResponse
  + is_error is false only for ArtifactValid and VerificationValid and true for LifecycleRefused or InputRefused

& [Metadata]
  + tool annotations are read-only nondestructive idempotent and closed-world
  + top-level input schema is strict and nested request is described as the complete Slice7 request object
  + output schema describes the structured response object without changing runtime response validation
  + server instructions preserve coherence-versus-truth and all effect non-authority

& [Acceptance]
  + direct server dispatch and official rmcp subprocess client list and call paths work
  + missing extra oversized and wrong tool inputs refuse before core mutation
  + response and summary are deterministic bounded and secret-free
  + focused debug release workspace lint format evidence and diff gates pass

& [NonGoals]
  + server state custody handles resources prompts HTTP auth installation host configuration model calls authoring repair runner signing global consumption admission installation deployment execution remote FPGA llama.cpp OneDrive EVO-X2 and Minecraft
